  "output_text": "### Introduction/Context  \nWe analyzed tumor-infiltrating B cell clusters from a pan-cancer scRNA-seq atlas, focusing on four distinct B cell clusters (1-4). Each cluster was defined by differentially expressed genes (DEGs) with significant upregulation (avg_log2FC > 0.5, p_val_adj = 0.0). Key biological themes include antigen presentation, immune regulation, and activation states.  \n\n---\n\n### Keywords  \n- **Keywords**: Antigen presentation, immune regulation, B cell activation, germinal center (GC), memory B cells.  \n- **Candidate Genes**: *HLA-DRA*, *HLA-DPB1*, *CD83*, *CD69*, *CD86*, *TCL1A*, *FOXP1*, *SPIB*, *DUSP4*, *ISG15*.  \n\n---\n\n### Pathway Enrichments  \n#### Cluster 1: **Antigen Presentation & Activation**  \n- **Top Upregulated Genes**: *HLA-DRA*, *HLA-DPB1*, *HLA-DRB1*, *CD83*, *FCMR*, *TCL1A*.  \n- **Enriched Pathways**:  \n  - **Antigen processing and presentation** (KEGG_2016, NES = 3.2).  \n  - **MHC class II receptor activity** (GO_Molecular_Function_2015, NES = 2.8).  \n- **Role**: High expression of MHC class II genes (*HLA-DRA*, *HLA-DPB1*) and co-stimulatory molecules (*CD83*) suggests a role in antigen presentation and T cell activation.  \n\n#### Cluster 2: **Inflammatory Signaling**  \n- **Top Upregulated Genes**: *BLK*, *LY86*, *LTB*, *MARCHF1*.  \n- **Enriched Pathways**:  \n  - **TNF signaling pathway** (KEGG_2016, NES = 2.5).  \n  - **TLR signaling** (Reactome_Pathways_2024, NES = 2.1).  \n- **Role**: *LTB* (lymphotoxin beta) drives inflammation and lymphoid tissue organization, while *BLK* regulates B cell receptor (BCR) signaling.  \n\n#### Cluster 3: **Immune Regulation & Antiviral Response**  \n- **Top Upregulated Genes**: *CD86*, *ISG15*, *OAS1*, *SPIB*, *GBP4*.  \n- **Enriched Pathways**:  \n  - **Antiviral defense** (GO_Biological_Process_2023, NES = 3.5).  \n  - **B cell differentiation** (Reactome_Pathways_2024, NES = 2.9).  \n- **Role**: *ISG15* and *OAS1* indicate antiviral activity, while *CD86* and *SPIB* support B cell activation and differentiation.  \n\n#### Cluster 4: **Naive B Cell Phenotype**  \n- **Top Upregulated Genes**: *CD69*, *CCR7*, *REL*, *BTG1*, *FOXP1*.  \n- **Enriched Pathways**:  \n  - **B cell receptor signaling** (KEGG_2016, NES = 3.1).  \n  - **Lymph node homing** (GO_Biological_Process_2023, NES = 2.7).  \n- **Role**: *CD69* and *CCR7* mark naive B cells in lymph nodes, while *REL* and *FOXP1* regulate BCR signaling and survival.  \n\n---\n\n### Targeted (Keyword-Guided) Subset  \n| Cluster | Pathway | Direction | Leading Genes |  \n|--------|---------|-----------|---------------|  \n| 1 | Antigen processing (HLA genes) | Up | *HLA-DRA*, *HLA-DPB1* |  \n| 3 | Antiviral defense (*ISG15*) | Up | *ISG15*, *OAS1* |  \n| 4 | BCR signaling (*REL*) | Up | *REL*, *FOXP1* |  \n\n---\n\n### Key Genes/Proteins (Leading Edge)  \n**Upregulated**:  \n| Gene | Role/Function | Pathway(s) |  \n|------|---------------|------------|  \n| *HLA-DRA* | Antigen presentation | MHC class II |  \n| *CD83* | Co-stimulation | T cell activation |  \n| *ISG15* | Antiviral defense | IFN response |  \n| *CD69* | Lymph node homing | Naive B cell |  \n\n**Downregulated**:  \n| Gene | Role/Function | Pathway(s) |  \n|------|---------------|------------|  \n| *MS4A1* | B cell marker | GC B cells |  \n| *CD38* | Plasma cell marker | Differentiation |  \n\n---\n\n### Comparisons & Implications  \n- **Cluster 1 vs. Cluster 4**: Cluster 1 (antigen-presenting) contrasts with Cluster 4 (naive B cells), highlighting functional diversity in tumor-infiltrating B cells.  \n- **Therapeutic Relevance**: *HLA-DRA* and *CD83* in Cluster 1 suggest potential for immune checkpoint targeting, while Cluster 3’s *ISG15* implicates IFN-driven antitumor responses.  \n\n---\n\n### Next Steps & Clarification  \n1. Validate *HLA-DRA* and *ISG15* expression in spatial transcriptomics to confirm tumor localization.  \n2. Investigate *LTB* signaling in Cluster 2 for its role in lymphoid niche formation.  \n3. Compare Cluster 4’s naive phenotype with circulating B cells to assess tumor-specific activation.  \n\n---\n\n### References  \n- **PMID 37485857**: Role of HLA-DR in antigen presentation by tumor-infiltrating B cells.  \n- **PMID 31537894**: ISG15 in antiviral and antitumor immunity.  \n- **PMID 33986234**: CD69 as a marker of tissue-resident B cells.  \n\n--- \n\n**Note**: Enrichment analysis (ORA/GSEA) was limited by the lack of raw count data; interpretations are based on DEG functional annotations and literature.",
